  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The photoelectric current from Na (work function, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>eV</mi></math>)&nbsp; is stopped by the output voltage of the cell</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Pt</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8214;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>bar</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>HCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>pH</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>AgCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8739;</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math><br />the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mi>H</mi></math> of aq. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi></math> required to stop the photoelectric current from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">w</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>eV</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, all other conditions remaining the same, is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> (to the nearest integer).</p><p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mfrac><mi>RT</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>06</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi>AgCl</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>Ag</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>22</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>",
